      <Desc>Community Inclusion Program: The Community Connections Program (CCP) team assesses, identifies, and trains participants on individual self-management and support strategies, seeks a multitude of inclusion opportunities, cooperatively discovers natural and meaningful community partners and friendship networks that could be relevant components and resources for the next stage of their lives. Specific activities include the following: Volunteering in community outreach venues to work on social and vocational skills such as food pantries, beach and park clean-ups, gardening projects, computer recycling programs. Shopping, cooking, and activities that build daily living skills. Accessing inclusive social, recreational, educational, and cultural venues. Building safety and community navigation skills in a variety of inclusive community settings. Participating in integrated recreational activities with neurotypical adults (clubs, community centers, recreation programs, libraries, YMCA, etc.) Visiting college and community college campuses, college sporting events, or other venues. Attending busy, integrative community festivals, sporting, and artistic events. Riding public transportation - the bus, trolley, trains, ferry, etc. to get to some community locations and promote independence. Eating in a variety of restaurants and cafes to practice dining skills. Attending museums, zoos, amusement parks and other educational San Diego venues.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>87028</ExpenseAmt>
        <GrantAmt>0</GrantAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>126035</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>Social Recreation: CCP's unique community-based social recreation program works with young adults with developmental disabilities that benefit from a specialized 1:1, 2:3, or 1:2 staff to participant ratioed level of support to successfully and safely engage in peer-inclusive, integrated social and recreational community settings. These settings include 1) Attending local community festivals, concerts, sporting and cultural events, 2)Joining in integrated college campus events, 3) Riding public transportation - the bus, trolley, trains, ferry, etc., 4)Participating in sport and recreational activities and venues such as community recreation centers, local YMCAs, public libraries, and other integrated program venues, 5) Dining in a variety of restaurants, cafes, community dining events, etc., 6) Accessing museums, zoos, amusement parks, and other unique San Diego venues.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
